  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/d82f445e19af6e6d343bfab6c082108e945a8feb21caa9b60a2d93da24fc3f6a.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the line segment directed along the $x$-axis. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5-1=4.\n$$",
